  "narrative": "Synthesis of the newly released validation evidence gives a bounded but clearer dataset-internal association picture. H120 is now discovery-plus-validation supported and therefore accepted and closed. Its discovery interaction estimate R108 was signed +1.087 with signed lower bound +0.899, and the independent validation R117 was signed +1.033 with signed lower bound +0.780. Both lower bounds are far above the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold. This supports the claim that the feature_010 higher-outcome association is attenuated in a broad feature_018 tail stratum, specifically after excluding feature_038 below -1. Because feature_038 and feature_018 are constructed correlated standardized assays, this should be interpreted as cross-assay tail heterogeneity of the feature_010 association, not as proof that feature_018 independently modifies outcome_001 after adjustment for feature_038, and not as a causal or generalizable mechanism claim. H100 remains unresolved and closed. Its discovery R78 was supportive, signed +0.590 with signed lower bound +0.338, but the independent validation R90 was not decisive: signed +0.360 with signed lower bound -0.036, below both null and the 0.15-unit threshold. The most defensible interpretation is that the unrestricted feature_038 interaction was diluted or partly distorted by inclusion of opposite-assay low-tail structure. The restricted high-feature_038 attenuation interaction H110 remains accepted with independent validation, and it is the preferable formulation for that feature_038-related attenuation pattern. H116 is closed as borderline unresolved because R94 is only marginally above threshold, signed +0.435 with lower bound +0.164, and it was a post-hoc reversed feature_010 mean difference. It should not be promoted without a more principled comparison or independent confirmation. The core supported main axes in this supplied dataset are now well delimited. feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 and therefore stronger composite dependency; this is large and validated, with discovery R21 signed +0.833 lower +0.767 and validation R37 signed +0.800 lower +0.706. feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 and therefore weaker composite dependency; this is large and validated, with discovery R20 signed +0.423 lower +0.327 and validation R50 signed +0.421 lower +0.293. feature_002=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 and therefore weaker composite dependency; this is large and validated, with discovery R48 signed +0.832 lower +0.766 and validation R63 signed +0.851 lower +0.756. The strongest heterogeneity finding is attenuation of the feature_010 association across standardized-research-signature tail structures. H110 supports high-feature_038 attenuation under sensitivity-restricted eligibility, discovery R91 +0.704 lower +0.431 and validation R103 +0.680 lower +0.280. H120 now supports broad feature_018 attenuation after excluding low feature_038. These two validated forms are complementary, but because feature_038 and feature_018 are correlated constructed assays, they localize the attenuation to the joint assay-tail structure rather than cleanly attributing it to one assay alone. Important negative findings constrain the final interpretation. H88, the feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction, was not supported: discovery R68 +0.210 lower +0.019 and validation R76 +0.017 lower -0.326. Thus the strong feature_002 and feature_010 main axes remain best described as largely separable associations in this dataset. H24 failed validation with signed estimate -0.041 and lower -0.159, and the broader feature_058 tail pattern in feature_036 remains unstable or null, including the H11/H12 evidence pattern. H49, the feature_003 contrast in the feature_037=0 and feature_010=0 joint stratum, failed both discovery threshold support and validation, with R32 +0.135 lower +0.064 and R104 +0.094 lower -0.001, so feature_003 is a weak candidate rather than a meaningful independent axis. The direct feature_037 and feature_002 tail-interaction tests H123 through H128 did not clear the threshold, so accepted subgroup mean differences for those axes should not be overinterpreted as evidence of threshold-supported assay-tail modification. The binary research markers and many simple binary screens have generally produced null or subthreshold results, further supporting a small number of central predictors. Remaining uncertainty is mainly about attribution and boundary of the feature_010 interaction pattern. The newly registered proposals directly test one-sided opposite-tail strata: feature_018-tail attenuation when feature_038 is nonpositive, and feature_038-tail attenuation when feature_018 is nonpositive. If those interactions remain above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed attenuation direction, the attenuation is less dependent on the other assay being high or merely excluding its low tail; if they fail, the validated claims should remain tied to the current eligibility-restricted formulations. The most useful next analyses are therefore these new conditional one-sided interaction tests, together with the still-active direct feature_037-by-feature_010 interactions H45/H46 and the joint-stratum persistence comparisons H129 through H132. If independent validation is used next, H122 is a good candidate because it is a broad feature_038 attenuation interaction accepted on discovery and directly complements the now validated broad feature_018 attenuation form H120. H117 remains a useful stricter feature_018 sensitivity formulation. All conclusions remain dataset-internal association claims: they do not establish causality, biological mechanism, biological role of feature_010, feature_037, feature_002, feature_018, or feature_038, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 synthesize final state. H120 accepted and closed on discovery plus independent validation: broad feature_018 attenuation of feature_010 after feature_038 >= -1; discovery lower +0.899, validation lower +0.780. H110 remains accepted/validated high-feature_038 attenuation interaction. H100 unresolved/closed: discovery supported but validation lower -0.036 below threshold/null; prefer restricted H110. H116 unresolved/closed: borderline lower +0.164, post-hoc reversed mean, do not promote. Validated core: feature_037=1 lower outcome_001/stronger dependency; feature_010=1 higher outcome_001/weaker dependency; feature_002=1 higher outcome_001/weaker dependency. Feature_010 heterogeneity is key: attenuation across correlated feature_038/feature_018 tail structure, not clean single-assay attribution. Negative/closed: H88 feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction; H24 feature_058 feature_036 tail; H49 feature_003 joint stratum; H123-H128 direct feature_037/feature_002 tail interactions; H114/H115 feature_036 feature_010 interactions; most binary marker screens null/subthreshold. Active accepted discovery-only cutoffs remain useful but redundant: H111/H117/H119/H121/H122. H122 is next validation candidate if budget, to confirm broad feature_038 attenuation. H117 is stricter feature_018 sensitivity candidate. New proposals registered for one-sided opposite-tail attribution: feature_018 attenuation when feature_038 <= 0, and feature_038 attenuation when feature_018 <= 0. Also analyze existing active H45/H46 feature_037-by-feature_010 interactions and H129-H132 joint-stratum persistence. Do not interpret as causal, mechanistic, gene-specific, or generalizable."
